# fixedbugs, defect 2317, 2026-11-07: a variant declaring one case name twice
# was told only that its `match` did not cover `.one`, which the arm names:
# the arm reached the second `one`, the first stayed uncovered, and the
# message was false. Now the second is refused where it stands, naming the
# first's line; the first is the case every arm and construction names, so
# the `match` is told nothing more.
variant Turn
    one
    two
    one  #~ case_declared_twice

function main()
    t: Turn = .one

    match t
        .one => print(1)
        .two => print(2)
